From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:11:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8180xp-dell-inspiron-3420: Move the ADSP
 firmware

The tree loads the GPU zap shader from qcom/sc8180xp/dell but the ADSP
firmware from the top of the firmware directory, as qcadsp8180.mbn.
Load it from qcom/sc8180xp/dell too, so the laptop's firmware package
installs both files in one folder and none at the top of /lib/firmware,
where another laptop's ADSP image of the same name could replace it.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180xp-dell-inspiron-3420.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180xp-dell-inspiron-3420.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180xp-dell-inspiron-3420.dts
index 7882d79..f4720c6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180xp-dell-inspiron-3420.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180xp-dell-inspiron-3420.dts
@@ -520,7 +520,7 @@ status="okay";
 
 &remoteproc_adsp {
    memory-region = <&adsp_mem>;
-   firmware-name= "qcadsp8180.mbn";
+   firmware-name= "qcom/sc8180xp/dell/qcadsp8180.mbn";
    status="okay";
 };
 
